","Scenario","Process","II.5"],["N048",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.5 Plan and manage procurement",13,"II.5 Plan and manage procurement","Medium","Before writing a formal bid request, a buyer wants to learn what solutions suppliers could offer. Which document should it issue?","Request for quotation (RFQ)","Request for information (RFI)","Purchase order","Contract change order","B","An RFI gathers information about supplier capabilities before an RFP or RFQ.","G5 original (prep-site topics, set 2)","","Predictive","Scenario","Process","II.5"],["P039",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.5 Plan and manage procurement",13,"II.5 Plan and manage procurement","Medium","In a predictive project, where would the project manager find the agreed terms for closing a contract with a vendor?","In the team charter","In the contract (agreement) itself","In the burndown chart","In the stakeholder register","B","Contract closure follows the terms and conditions in the agreement.","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Predictive","Scenario","Process","II.5"],["P040",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.5 Plan and manage procurement",13,"II.5 Plan and manage procurement","Hard","A buyer wants vendor prices for a clearly defined, standard product, and the choice will be based mainly on price. Which procurement document fits best?","Request for information (RFI)","Request for proposal (RFP)","Request for quotation (RFQ)","Work performance report","C","An RFQ asks for prices on a well-defined item; an RFP asks for solutions to complex needs; an RFI gathers information.","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Predictive","Scenario","Process","II.5"],["P049",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.5 Plan and manage procurement",13,"II.5 Plan and manage procurement","Hard","A vendor and the buyer disagree about whether extra work is covered by the contract. What is generally the preferred way to settle the claim?","Going to court immediately","Ignoring the claim until the vendor gives up","Paying whatever the vendor asks","