Medium","A CPI of 0.80 means:","Each 1 SAR spent earns 0.80 SAR of work","The project is 80% complete","Costs are 20% below plan","The project is 20% ahead of schedule","A","CPI below 1 means the work is costing more than planned.","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["B097",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","BAC = 50,000 and CPI = 1.25. Using EAC = BAC / CPI, what is the EAC?","40,000","48,750","50,000","62,500","A","EAC = 50,000 / 1.25 = 40,000.","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Calculation","Process","II.6"],["B098",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","BAC = 20,000 and EAC = 25,000. What is the variance at completion (VAC)?","−5,000","0.80","1.25","+5,000","A","VAC = BAC − EAC = 20,000 − 25,000 = −5,000.","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Calculation","Process","II.6"],["B101",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","Which index shows how efficiently the remaining work must be done to finish on the original budget?","PV","CV","TCPI","SPI","C","TCPI = (BAC − EV) / (BAC − AC).","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["B102",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Medium","Money set aside for identified risks and included in the cost baseline is the:","Earned value","Management reserve","Contingency reserve","Sunk cost","C","Contingency reserves cover known-unknowns inside the baseline.","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["B104",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","Money held by management for unidentified risks, outside the cost baseline, is the:","Contingency reserve","Management reserve","Planned value","Budget at completion","B","Management reserve covers unknown-unknowns and sits outside the baseline.","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["B106",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Medium","A cost variance of −3,000 means:","The project is ahead of schedule","The project is under budget by 3,000","The project is over budget by 3,000","The project is behind schedule","C","A negative CV means actual cost is higher than earned value.","G5 original (new)","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["N021",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Medium","Early in a project, the cost estimate is given as a wide range. As the project progresses, the range should:","Stay exactly the same","Become wider","Be replaced by a single exact figure from day one","Narrow as more information becomes available","D","Estimates are progressively elaborated; accuracy improves as uncertainty falls.","G5 original (prep-site topics, set 2)","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["N042",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","Midway through the project, the sponsor announces a 20% funding cut. What should the project manager do first?","Analyse options with the sponsor, such as reducing scope or re-phasing, and update the plan through change control","Continue as planned and hope for more money","Quietly cut quality testing","Stop the project without consulting anyone","A","Funding shortfalls are handled by analysing options with decision makers and changing the baseline formally.","G5 original (prep-site topics, set 2)","","Predictive","Scenario","Process","II.6"],["P050",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Medium","A task has a budget of $10,000. It is 40% complete and has cost $5,000 so far. What is the cost variance (CV)?","−$1,000","+$1,000","−$5,000","+$4,000","A","EV = 40% × $10,000 = $4,000. CV = EV − AC = $4,000 − $5,000 = −$1,000 (over budget).","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Predictive","Calculation","Process","II.6"],["P051",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","BAC = $100,000, EV = $40,000 and AC = $50,000. The overrun was a one-time event and the rest of the work is expected at the budgeted rate. What is the EAC?","$125,000","$110,000","$100,000","$90,000","B","For an atypical variance, EAC = AC + (BAC − EV) = $50,000 + $60,000 = $110,000. ($125,000 would assume the CPI continues.)","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Predictive","Calculation","Process","II.6"],["P052",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Medium","A project's EAC is $125,000 and its actual cost to date is $50,000. What is the estimate to complete (ETC)?","$175,000","$50,000","$125,000","$75,000","D","ETC = EAC − AC = $125,000 − $50,000 = $75,000.","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Predictive","Calculation","Process","II.6"],["P054",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Hard","BAC = $100,000, EV = $40,000 and AC = $50,000. What TCPI is needed to finish within the original budget?","1.20","0.80","0.83","1.00","A","TCPI = (BAC − EV) ÷ (BAC − AC) = $60,000 ÷ $50,000 = 1.20, so remaining work must be done 20% more efficiently.","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Predictive","Calculation","Process","II.6"],["Q41",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Easy","Which formula gives the cost performance index (CPI)?","EV ÷ AC","EV ÷ PV","AC ÷ EV","PV ÷ EV","A","CPI = EV ÷ AC. SPI = EV ÷ PV.","Team v1","","Predictive","Knowledge","Process","II.6"],["Q43",true,"Bank",2,"Process","II.6 Plan and manage finance",14,"II.6 Plan and manage finance","Medium","EV = SAR 6,000 and AC = SAR 6,600. What is the cost variance (CV)?","+SAR 600 – under budget","–SAR 600 – over budget","–SAR 600 – under budg