upport organizational change","Medium","After an old system is retired, but before people are comfortable with the new one, staff feel confused and less productive. What should the project manager do?","Support people through the transition with clear communication, training and quick wins","Bring back the old system","Do nothing, since productivity will recover by itself","Replace the staff who are struggling","A","Change models (such as Satir or Bridges) describe this dip; leaders support people through it.","G5 original (prep-site topics, set 2)","","Any","Scenario","Business Environment","III.7"],["P057",true,"Bank",3,"Business Environment","III.7 Support organizational change",25,"III.7 Support organizational change","Medium","After several members used to predictive work join an agile team, customer satisfaction drops. What should the agile coach do first?","Switch the whole project to a predictive approach","Coach the new members on agile values and practices","Remove the new members from the team","Stop the customer reviews","B","New members need help adopting the agile mindset; changing the whole approach is not the first response.","G5 original (prep-site topics)","","Agile","Scenario","Business Environment","III.7"],["S033",true,"Bank",3,"Business Environment","III.7 Support organizational change",25,"III.7 Support organizational change","Medium","An organisation is moving from predictive to agile delivery, and middle managers are resisting the change. What should the project manager do first?","Report them to senior management","Exclude them from all project decisions","Pause the agile adoption permanently","Understand their concerns, explain the benefits, and involve them in shaping the new ways of working","D","Supporting organisational change starts with understanding the culture and engaging those affected.","G5 original (PMP 2026 scenario)","","Hybrid","Scenario","Business Environment","III.7"],["B110",true,"Bank",3,"Business Environment","III.8 Eva